# Workspace Recipe Docs

Inspect, validate, preview, and render recipes.

## When To Use It

- Before creating shaped files.
- After editing recipe manifests or templates.
- Between rule validation and root health.
- When checking modules against mapped recipe roles.

## How To Respond

- List and show recipes before rendering.
- Use `enclosure workspace recipe <name> <path> --shell` as the first-run convention oracle.
- Use dry runs before writing.
- Compose reusable `fragment` recipes with `includes`.
- Keep module-to-role ownership in `workspace.recipe.roles_map`.
- Use `--drifts` to compare mapped module trees to recipes.
- Use `--bench <module> --html <path>` for strict module warp.
- Use `--bench-all --html <path>` for the strict workspace warp index.

## Related Commands

- `enclosure workspace recipe --help`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --list`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --check`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --bench <module> --html <path>`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --bench-all --html <path>`
- `enclosure workspace rules --docs`
